emullins@hydra.unm.edu (Eric Mullins) writes:
>
>Having been caught myself by a cockatrice corpse years ago, I have always
>kept !pickup in my NETHACKOPTIONS.

This is good advice, and it will usually protect a player from
cockatrice corpses, but only if the player can see.  It seems that
blind people can't help feeling around on the ground at each move in
nethack.

You are right that !pickup is a good option.  If there is no warning
before picking up a cockatrice corpse, then it is interesting to
speculate on why !pickup is not the default option.  Historically, in
nethack's predecessor, rogue, !pickup was not an option.  Players had
to pick up whatever they stepped on, which was usually good because a
player had to race around to avoid starving or getting smashed by
xorns.  Thus, the current default of pickup can be seen as a holdover
from a game that did not have cockatrice corpses.

It would be interesting to consider changing the default to !pickup in
nethack.  Such play would undoubtedly affect other aspects of the
game, like food consumption.  Tweaking some constants might keep
players from starving because of the extra turns taken to pick up
items.  If that is done, does it make sense for moving and picking up
to take more turns then just moving?  If so, then people could not
save turns by turning on pickup, though they might save some typing,
especially if they have gloves on.  The same question seems to be
appropriate for monsters as well.

